WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.780
One of the highlights of football was LSU took a trip to Indiana,

2
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:17.380
I forgot the year but it must have been about 1925 or ’26 or something [it was 1924].

3
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:24.480
But we played Indiana [University] and of course the student body couldn’t go,

4
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:36.640
but they had a place downtown and also in the community club where somebody called the game and we . . . The first play of the game,

5
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.060
LSU fumbled the football and Indiana made a touchdown.

6
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:51.580
But after that, we made a comeback and won the game by nineteen to seventeen or something like that.

7
00:00:51.580 --> 00:01:01.400
When the team got back to Baton Rouge . . . The railroad station was at the foot of North Boulevard just near the Mississippi River.

8
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.980
It’s now the Louisiana Arts and Science Museum.

9
00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.880
Oh, Baton Rouge went absolutely wild.

10
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.280
The students were all so wild.

11
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:24.680
And we just decided to have a holiday and we didn’t need any encouragement because we just did it anyhow.

12
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:35.200
And we marched down Third Street yelling and hollering and everybody in Baton Rouge just joined in.

13
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:53.000
Another trip, [in 1931] Huey Long decided he was going to fix it so the boys could . . . the student body could follow the team to play Army in New York.
